& [ImplementedPlaneSet] is complete for the signed pure-form frontier
  + governance and planning forms include TaskContract, objective, dependency, constraint, alternative, PlanRevision, ScheduleCandidate, Commitment, and WakeCondition
  + temporal forms include domain-aware TimeExpression, recurrence, CalendarItem, authority, lifecycle, provider-sync, sensitivity, and disclosure states
  + repository forms include materiality, ContentObject, MaterialEvent, SemanticSnapshot, RepositoryGeneration, and non-authoritative GitProjection
  + transition forms include DeclaredIntent, eight disjoint DiffKinds, InvalidationEdge, ChangeCapsule, and legal capsule-state transitions
  + lane forms include cursor, immutable message, work packet, ReflectionReturn, ObserverJoin, ReleaseBarrier, bounded lag, and legal lane transitions
  + compiler forms include CompilerGeneration, explicit forward and rear stages, independent correspondence evidence, and CompilerImpact
  + learning forms include ForecastError, PlanDeviation, SemanticSurprise, LessonCandidate, and TrainingExampleCandidate without adoption behavior

& [NormalizationAndValidation] are deterministic and fail closed
  + all unordered collections use BTreeMap or BTreeSet canonical ordering
  + to_normalized_temporal_form validates before emitting compact canonical JSON
  + from_normalized_temporal_form rejects malformed JSON, unknown fields, unsupported versions, invalid identities, invalid content, and valid but noncanonical JSON
  + the aggregate validator binds map key to record identity and checks locally governed cross-record references
  + time domains, recurrence bounds, snapshot non-atomicity, Git non-authority, lifecycle ordering, complete admitted diff accounting, exact reflection generation, join completeness, release barriers, bounded lag, and independent compiler correspondence fail closed
  + the aggregate record count and text size are bounded

& [ImmutabilityMeaning] is explicit
  + records carry stable identity plus revision or generation identity and predecessor references
  + APIs transform or validate values and contain no persistence or mutation command
  + failed and superseded states remain representable rather than overwritten
  + immutable means versioned value semantics at this ABI boundary and does not claim that Rust prevents a caller from binding a value mutably in local memory

& [ModuleSizeDisposition] is deliberate
  + the 1940-line module is predominantly closed vocabulary and declarative schema for one versioned ABI plus its colocated pure invariants
  + one surface currently improves review of field vocabulary against the canonical specification and avoids premature cross-module dependency cycles
  + [refactor_trigger] is behavior enters the module, one plane changes independently, compile latency becomes material, or review evidence shows navigation loss
  - never: use the present file size as authority to add runtime behavior to the schema module

& [DeliberateLimit] is binding
  + no Planner search, Calendar behavior, recurrence expansion, event append, snapshot materialization, CompareAndAppend, lane execution, compiler pass, lesson adoption, or replay is implemented
  + no clock, filesystem, Git command, database, network, service, thread, provider, notification, model, ECS runtime, tool invocation, desktop, FPGA, or external effect is reachable
